THE §73 TREATMENT, AS A REVERSIBLE PATCH.

APPLY IT IN REVERSE on the landing commit and you get COLUMN B -- the FAITHFUL
transliteration of `5403671558`'s 8F ghost family, live `ready` pin and all:

    git apply -R sw/testdata/relanding/ghost8f_treatment.patch

That tree FAILS `sw/r7_lint.py` by construction (3 undeclared carriers, 7
`stop` sites) and is NOT landable; it exists so the A/B of
`docs/notes/ghost8f_prereg_2026-08-09.md` §5 is re-runnable.  `sw/ss_lint.py`'s
constants do NOT move between the two forms, so nothing else needs reverting.

The three parts, all documented in the RTL beside the code they change:
  P2a  the four published rails read `r_ready_prev`, not the bare pin
  P2b  `acc_split_wr` -- the write accounting's own ghost-free split
  P2c  S_PRERD's ghost-late arm writes only register `D` pins

MEASURED B vs C: identical on every gate; six OPEN_BUS seeds' row streams
differ (fz2c/410008, fz2e/518004, 519016, 520000, 520040, 522029).
